  "body": "## Why\n\nPlan PR 2b: the fixture workbench is too much machine for the TUI MVP. Keep one SQLite hub, sessions, idempotent commands, `bf doctor` / `bf serve` / `bf web`.\n\n## What\n\n- Delete jobs/delivery/verification/fixtures/qualification/forge/domain/protocol, `src/bin/`, `fixtures/`, `schemas/`, migrations 002/003, hardening/acceptance, `scripts/generate-contracts`\n- Rewrite `001_core.sql` to principals/sessions/commands/operations\n- Trim hub/commands/api/storage/main\n- Drop `ts-rs`, `reqwest`, `async-stream`\n- `tests/core.rs`: lock, sqlite pin, HTTP auth + command replay\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- `cargo test --locked` green\n- `wc -l src/*.rs` keepers = **1085** (\u2264 1100)\n- `cargo tree` lines **171** (was ~281 with the dropped crates)\n- `bash scripts/check` EXIT 0 (node 22.23.2 / npm 10.9.8)\n- `main.rs` verbs: `doctor`, `serve`, `web` (bare `bf` opens web until the TUI PR)\n\nDoes **not** include PR3 stubs (`src/agents.rs`, `board.rs`, `tui/`, `AGENTS.md`). Those stay untracked for the CLI-skeleton lane.\n\n## Review\n\nAuthor vendor: **grok**. Reviewer must be a different vendor (claude or cursor). Then `gh pr merge --rebase --delete-branch`.\n\nbf-author: grok/grok-4.6\nbf-claim: AGENT_CHAT.md 2026-09-18 grok PR2b",
